{"name":"Zebra Grass","hex":"#9da286","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"zebra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of three species of subgenus Hippotigris: Equus grevyi, Equus quagga, or Equus zebra, all with black and white stripes and native to Africa.","A referee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zebra"},{"term":"grass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the family Poaceae, characterized by leaves that arise from nodes in the stem and leaf bases that wrap around the stem, especially those grown as ground cover rather than for grain.","Any of the various plants that are not in the family Poaceae that resemble grasses."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lay out on the grass; to knock down (an opponent etc.).","To act as a grass or informer, to betray; to report on (criminals etc) to the authorities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Miscanthus sinensis","blocks":[{"text":"Miscanthus sinensis, also called eulalia grass, Chinese silver grass, or elephant grass, is a species of flowering plant in the grass family Poaceae, native to most of East Asia and Southeast Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Japanese_pampas_grass_%E3%82%B9%E3%82%B9%E3%82%AD%E3%81%AE%E7%A9%82%E6%B3%A2PB080105.jpg/330px-Japanese_pampas_grass_%E3%82%B9%E3%82%B9%E3%82%AD%E3%81%AE%E7%A9%82%E6%B3%A2PB080105.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miscanthus_sinensis","wikidata":"Q1073621"},{"title":"Zebra","blocks":[{"text":"Zebras are African equines with distinctive black-and-white striped coats. There are three living species: Grévy's zebra, the plains zebra, and the mountain zebra. Zebras share the genus Equus with horses and asses, the three groups being the only living members of the family Equidae. Zebra stripes come in different patterns, unique to each individual. Several theories have been proposed for the function of these patterns, with most evidence supporting them as a deterrent for biting flies. Zebras inhabit eastern and southern Africa and can be found in a variety of habitats such as savannahs, grasslands, woodlands, shrublands, and mountainous areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Plains_Zebra_Equus_quagga_cropped.jpg/330px-Plains_Zebra_Equus_quagga_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zebra","wikidata":"Q32789"},{"title":"Grass","blocks":[{"text":"Grass refers to various families of plants. The three major families of grasslike plants are true grasses (Poaceae), sedges (Cyperaceae), and rushes (Juncaceae). Lawns and pasturelands are typically composed of true grasses, five of which cover 46% of the world's arable land: rice, wheat, maize, barley, and sugar cane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Poa_annua.jpg/330px-Poa_annua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass","wikidata":"Q643352"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Tonomine_highland_%E7%A0%A5%E5%B3%B0%E9%AB%98%E5%8E%9F%EF%BC%88%E5%85%B5%E5%BA%AB%E7%9C%8C%E7%A5%9E%E5%B4%8E%E9%83%A1%E7%A5%9E%E6%B2%B3%E7%94%BA%EF%BC%89PA240025.JPG/500px-Tonomine_highland_%E7%A0%A5%E5%B3%B0%E9%AB%98%E5%8E%9F%EF%BC%88%E5%85%B5%E5%BA%AB%E7%9C%8C%E7%A5%9E%E5%B4%8E%E9%83%A1%E7%A5%9E%E6%B2%B3%E7%94%BA%EF%BC%89PA240025.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Tonomine_highland_%E7%A0%A5%E5%B3%B0%E9%AB%98%E5%8E%9F%EF%BC%88%E5%85%B5%E5%BA%AB%E7%9C%8C%E7%A5%9E%E5%B4%8E%E9%83%A1%E7%A5%9E%E6%B2%B3%E7%94%BA%EF%BC%89PA240025.JPG/1280px-Tonomine_highland_%E7%A0%A5%E5%B3%B0%E9%AB%98%E5%8E%9F%EF%BC%88%E5%85%B5%E5%BA%AB%E7%9C%8C